In a project that depends on AppDimens (appdimens-*, webdimens, Bodenberg.AppDimens.*, AppDimens.Net), before writing or converting UI sizes:

1. Base screen: use `appdimens.config.json → design.baseScreen`; else one unambiguous source (single design frame, ≥ 80 % of previews from `node .appdimens/tools/appdimens-kit/cli.mjs detect .`, platform default for new screens) stated as "assumed, unconfirmed"; else ask (one message, ≤ 5 questions).
2. Never re-label a number (`16.dp` → `16.sdp` grows 20–47 % on phones). Convert with `node .appdimens/tools/appdimens-kit/cli.mjs normalize --device <base> --strategy <s> <values…>` (`--theme` for theme tokens, `--xml` for Android XML, `--axis h` for hdp, `--density` for px frames).
3. Decide each element's intent (role, fill/hug, scroll, fixed) before choosing tokens. Hairlines, elevation, shadows and platform chrome stay fixed; touch targets: visual size is a token, the hit area uses the platform API.
4. Follow the full rule `appdimens-layout-intent` and the platform rule; validate with `node .appdimens/tools/appdimens-kit/cli.mjs lint <files>`.
